## IGNITE CAPSTONE

## Bringing in the Data and Setting up the Library

```{r}
library(tidyverse)
library(readxl)
library(dplyr)
library(lme4)
library(lmerTest)
library(ggpubr)
library(googlesheets4)

#IGNITE_Data_Sheet <- read_excel("IGNITE Data Sheet.xlsx", 
   #                             sheet = "RCoding")

IGNITE_Data_Sheet<-googlesheets4::read_sheet("https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1Z7aurgQzPtNckHCvg0PXA97xKa3VXuFM_nTSHRgTMcY/edit?gid=125710380#gid=125710380", sheet = "RCoding")
```

Data is already really clean, will save the chunk below in case of data cleaning

```{r}
#data cleaning here!
#There is one reading of black mustard that is 600 FMC, will take that out

IGNITE_Data_Sheet_2 <- IGNITE_Data_Sheet |> 
  filter(Sample_ID != "2_BRNI_261027_1",
         Sample_ID != "3_BRNI_261027_1" ,
         Sample_ID != "4_BRNI_261027_3")|> 
  mutate(Site = as.factor(Site))



```

Exploratory Data Graphing

```{r}
